  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given a positive integer XXX, find the **smallest** positive integer YYY satisfying all of the following conditions:\n\n\nYYY should not be a prime;\nYYY should not be a perfect square;\nNo factor of YYY other than 111 is less than XXX.\nNote that YYY might not fit in a 323232 bit integer.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of a positive integer XXX as mentioned in the statement.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the **smallest** positive integer YYY satisfying the given conditions.\n\n\nNote that YYY might not fit in a 323232 bit integer.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤51 \\leq T \\leq 51≤T≤5",
      "1≤X≤1091 \\leq X \\leq 10^91≤X≤109"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n1\n2\n3",
        "output": "6\n6\n15",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Let us consider all values of YYY in increasing order:\n\nY=2Y = 2Y=2: It is a prime.\nY=3Y = 3Y=3: It is a prime.\nY=4Y = 4Y=4: It is a perfect square (4=22)(4 = 2^2)(4=22).\nY=5Y = 5Y=5: It is a prime.\nY=6Y = 6Y=6: It is neither prime, nor a perfect square. The non-111 factors of 666 are 2,32, 32,3 and 666, none of which are less than X=1X = 1X=1.\n\nThus, 666 is the smallest integer satisfying the given conditions.\nTest case 222: Y=6Y = 6Y=6 has non-111 factors 2,3,2, 3,2,3, and 666, none of which are less than X=2X = 2X=2.\nTest case 333: The smallest integer satisfying the conditions is 151515. The non-111 factors of 151515 are 3,53, 53,5 and 151515, none of which are less than X=3X = 3X=3."
      }
    ]
  },
